            <ArticleTitle>High-speed rotational atherectomy of tortuous coronary arteries with guidewire-associated pseudostenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of high-speed rotational atherectomy cases is discussed in which pseudostenosis was noted following initial guidewire placement. The results and technical considerations when using the Rotablator in the setting of guidewire-induced pseudostenosis are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
